      <!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
      <para>
        The topic covers the basics of PCP.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <para>
    Performance data is collected by <emphasis>performance metrics domain
    agents</emphasis> (PMDAs), one per subsystem such as the kernel, disks, or
    a database. Each PMDA passes its metrics to the
    <systemitem class="daemon">pmcd</systemitem> daemon, which is the single
    point of contact every other PCP tool talks to. <command>pmlogger</command>
    is the tool that turns those live metrics into an archive you can query
    later, and <command>pminfo</command> queries them directly, without
    logging anything.
  </para>
</topic>
